# Build DAG — Payload Models Reference

**Endpoint:** `POST /build_dag`  
**Service:** `dag_service_latest.py` v1.3  

---

## BuildDagPayload (top-level)

```jsonc
{
  "run_control_id": "string",
  "triggerType": "string",
  "schedule": "string | null",
  "executionSteps": [ ...Node ],
  "nodes": [ ...Node ]
}
```

| Field | Type | Required | Accepted Values | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `run_control_id` | string | **Yes** | any non-empty string | Sanitized to lowercase and used to create Airflow `dag_id` as `<sanitized_run_control_id>_dag`. Cannot be null or blank |
| `triggerType` | string | No | `"0"`-`"4"` or `"O"`, `"S"`, `"F"`, `"D"`, `"R"` | Numeric values are mapped internally to their letter equivalents. This field does not control the generated schedule |
| `schedule` | string \| null | No | Airflow-compatible schedule string | Any non-empty value is emitted as the DAG schedule, regardless of `triggerType` |
| `executionSteps` | array of Node | Yes* | array | Preferred field name for node list |
| `nodes` | array of Node | Yes* | array | Alias for `executionSteps`. Both accepted and merged internally |

> *At least one node required across `executionSteps` + `nodes` combined.

---

## Node (each item in executionSteps / nodes)

```json
{
  "id": "string",
  "name": "string",
  "executor_build_id": "string",
  "engine": "PYTHON",
  "executor_order_id": 1,
  "executor_sequence_id": 1,
  "execution_mode": "sync",
  "branch_on_status": false,
  "on_success_node_ids": [],
  "on_failure_node_ids": []
}
```

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | string | No | Auto: `task1`, `task2`... | Internal wiring ID. Used in `on_success_node_ids` / `on_failure_node_ids` references. Never shown in Airflow UI. **Must be set explicitly when using branching.** |
| `name` | string | **Yes** | — | Shown as the task label in Airflow graph view. If same name appears in multiple layers it is auto-deduplicated as `name_order_seq` |
| `executor_build_id` | string | **Yes** | — | The key the task uses at **run time** to look up its HTTP parameters from `dag_run.conf`. Not the same as `id` or `name` |
| `engine` | string | **Yes** | — | Any non-empty string is accepted and included as metadata. Generated execution remains HTTP/Python-based |
| `executor_order_id` | integer ≥ 1 | **Yes** | — | Layer number. Same-layer nodes may run in parallel. Cross-layer wiring follows the sequence-based rules below |
| `executor_sequence_id` | integer ≥ 1 | **Yes** | — | Position within a layer. No two nodes can share the same `(executor_order_id, executor_sequence_id)` pair |
| `execution_mode` | string | No | `"sync"` | See execution mode table below |
| `branch_on_status` | boolean | No | `false` | Set `true` to route downstream tasks based on the node's final execution status. At least one branch target is required |
| `on_success_node_ids` | array of string | Required if branching | `[]` | List of `id` values selected when the node's branch marker is `success` |
| `on_failure_node_ids` | array of string | Required if branching | `[]` | List of `id` values selected when the node's branch marker is missing, failed, or otherwise not `success` |

---

## Execution Mode

| Value | Waits for response | Fails DAG on non-2xx | Can branch |
|---|---|---|---|
| `sync` | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| `async_no_wait` | Yes: submits, then polls status until terminal | Yes, when polling returns a failure/unknown/timeout result | Yes |
| `fire_and_forget` | Waits only for the initial HTTP submission response | Yes, when the initial submission is non-2xx or raises | No |

---

## triggerType Mapping

| Payload value | Internal code | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `"0"` | `O` | On-demand |
| `"1"` | `S` | Scheduled (cron) |
| `"2"` | `F` | Reserved |
| `"3"` | `D` | Reserved |
| `"4"` | `R` | Reserved |

> The current service does not enforce a relationship between `triggerType` and `schedule`. A non-empty `schedule` produces a scheduled DAG even when `triggerType` is omitted or set to `"0"`.

---

## Validation Rules (enforced at build time — 422 on failure)

| Rule | Detail |
|---|---|
| `run_control_id` required | Cannot be null, empty, or whitespace |
| At least one node | `executionSteps` + `nodes` combined must have ≥ 1 node |
| Unique `id` | No two nodes can have the same `id` after auto-assignment |
| Unique `(order, seq)` pair | No two nodes can share `executor_order_id` + `executor_sequence_id` |
| Branch references must exist | `on_success_node_ids` and `on_failure_node_ids` must point to `id` values that exist in the same payload |
| `branch_on_status: true` requires targets | At least one target across `on_success_node_ids` and `on_failure_node_ids` must be present. Configure both lists when both outcomes must continue |
| No overlap between success and failure lists | A node cannot appear in both lists of the same parent |
| `fire_and_forget` cannot branch | `execution_mode: fire_and_forget` with `branch_on_status: true` is rejected |
| No cycles | Circular dependencies via `executor_order_id` layers or branch targets are rejected |
| Non-empty string fields | `executor_build_id`, `engine`, and `name` cannot be null or blank |

