## Topology Index

| # | Topology | Key fields |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Single node | 1 node, no branching |
| 2 | Linear chain | N nodes, sequential layers |
| 3 | Scheduled linear chain | `triggerType: "1"` + cron |
| 4 | Parallel (same layer) — structural | Multiple nodes share `executor_order_id` |
| 5 | Parallel then merge — structural | Parallel layer feeds one merge node |
| 6 | Conditional branch — success only | `branch_on_status: true`, `on_success_node_ids` only |
| 7 | Conditional branch — failure only | `branch_on_status: true`, `on_failure_node_ids` only |
| 8 | Conditional branch — both paths | `branch_on_status: true`, success + failure each route to different nodes |
| 9 | Conditional branch — parallel success split | Success routes to multiple nodes that then merge |
| 10 | Orphan node | Non-final node with no downstream children, auto-wired to `finalize_results` |
| 11 | Mixed execution modes | `sync` + `async_no_wait` + `fire_and_forget` in one DAG |
| 12 | Multi-layer with parallel and branch | Full real-world pipeline |
| 13 | Conditional branch inside parallel layer | Two parallel nodes, one branches |
| 14 | Chained branches (branch after branch) | Branch node downstream is itself a branch node |
| 15 | Conditional branch into three nodes, then merge | Success selects three parallel nodes; success and failure paths merge |

